  testing process for anyone wanting to  own a football club  it's a difficult one because they do  have they did have this sort of  wanting to uh establish separation so  it's the public investment fund of saudi  arabia that has allegedly bought new  castle united  and  there was the question last year because  this was muted last year there was a  question last year of whether or not  that meant that the kingdom of saudi  arabia which runs the investment fund or  or there is a  blurred line there are they actually  going to be the ones that are running  newcastle united now i i understand that  that issue of separation has now been  settled because that was the key part of  arbitration that newcastle united was  going to go to in january  if that's the case then then there is a  bit of a moral sort of ethical question  um being asked and being answered um  but i i kind of i kind of sort of  bristle a little bit at the idea that it  should be  up to a sport sort of to to to be the  moral and ethical arbiters of of  buyers i don't know i don't know the  answer to it no no it's a it's a  complicated issue and like you said when  it comes to you know qatar hosting the  world cup for example or you know  as we said boxing being held in saudi  arabia these conversations keep coming  up but somehow it continues and just  gets brushed under the carpet it's just  reared its head again so it was  interesting to get your point of view  charlotte um let's end on an upbeat note  if this takeover goes through today it's  not just transformative for your club  yeah fingers crossed it's not just just  transformative for your club but it's  transformative for the city as well  because for those who are watching who  aren't football fans but may well have  been to newcastle so jason's park is  right at the heart  of newcastle if you're shopping in  newcastle on a saturday afternoon a gold  coasin you can hear the cheers from the  shops it's very much  newcastle so how transformative is it  going to be for the city as well as the  club charlotte  literally giving me goosebumps saying  that by the way  um i it's huge it's it's massive and  as you mentioned at the start of this  interview  the the pockets of this these people are  very deep  and so  and they've also already made the right  noises about investment in community  investment in the academy investment in  the ground the the stadium needs  upgrades it needs a new roof it needs  paint it needs you know all kinds of  things and and so  and so for that sort of investment to  start happening i just think the region  is going to benefit i think  you look at the geographical um  potential of fans coming to newcastle  united and to newcastle  there isn't another club another premier  league club until going south until you  get to leeds there's nothing going west  there's scotland north  there's nothing else so there's so much  potential for the region to really sort  of benefit from this and that really  excites me because  newcastle united is rooted in its  community and i'm very proud to be part  of that community and  i just  the potential now is huge that certainly  is um charlotte let's hope it's a double  celebration for you at this wedding this  weekend are the bride and groom  newcastle united fans by any chance  no they're not they're londoners  unfortunately oh  well hopefully  hopefully they'll be pleased enough for  you for you to wear your newcastle  united shirt to the wedding should this  take over deal go through today uh  charlotte thank you so much charlotte  robson uh from the newcastle united  supporters trust ahead of that proposed  takeover by a saudi arabia consortium we  hear it's going to go through before the  end of the day

